    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: I have decided this case on the route-deviation policy, which is the category it was filed under, and every figure below is read off the record so both of you can check it.\n\nThe governing measurement is the GPS trace. EV-GPS-00715 is unimpaired — 100% coverage, 55 fixes at the published 10-second cadence, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 s — so no POL-RD-07 issue arises and nothing has to be reconstructed across a gap. The trace shows the vehicle covered 3.4 km (trace_distance_km) against a booked optimal route of 6.4 km (trip_record.optimal_distance_km). The excess is 3.4 − 6.4 = −3.0 km, i.e. −46.9%. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is greater than 20% of the optimal distance and greater than 0.8 km; a negative excess fails both tests, so no deviation exists and the clause directs NO_ACTION however the trip is characterised.\n\nThat closes the distance-and-time route. This was an upfront-quoted trip (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE on EV-FARE-00715), so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available. The only route-deviation money is the POL-RD-11(a) amount by which charged_total exceeds the quote plus the properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines. Charged_total is SGD 7.20, quoted_fare_sgd is SGD 7.20, and there are no ERP gantry lines (SGD 0.00), no airport surcharge, and a waiting-time fee of SGD 0.00, so that amount computes to SGD 0.00 — the fare artifact itself publishes pol_rd_11_remedy 0.00. I have also checked POL-RD-09: with no charge line the trace never crossed and no surcharge on a trip that does not originate at an airport, there is no billing-integrity correction and no POL-RD-09(4) referral.\n\nThe rider's account of what happened is not in dispute and I accept it. The driver's own in-app message at 12:25:40, \"Hospital too far in this jam. I will end here and refund you.\", and the trip record's dropoff label, \"Shelter where service ended\", show the trip was ended short of the hospital. But no clause in this policy turns an unfinished trip into a refund: the route-deviation clauses measure excess over the optimal route, not distance left undriven, and the upfront rules fix the fare at booking and close the distance-and-time route. The driver's \"in this jam\" explanation does him no good either — the only traffic advisory for the trip, EV-ADVIS-00715-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run on this record and, per POL-RD-13, an uncited traffic assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Nothing here decides against the rider's honesty; the route-deviation rules simply provide no money for these facts.\n\nNo clause in this policy produces a referral, and no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the trace is unimpaired, no timestamps conflict, no exculpatory clause has been invoked against a cited artifact, and no charge line lacks a counterpart. The disputed SGD 7.20 therefore stands as charged: fare_breakdown.payment_status (CHARGED) and refund_issued_sgd (0.00) are left as they are.\n\nOne open question, which belongs here rather than in any referral: the record shows you were carried 3.4 km of a 6.4 km journey and charged the full upfront fare of SGD 7.20, and the driver told you in writing that a refund was coming. That may well be worth pursuing, but it is not a route deviation and this policy gives me no power over it. If you wish to take it further, raise it directly with support as a trip-completion or service dispute."
  },
